WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.092
The Python lab follows one consistent logic.

00:00:03.092 --> 00:00:06.902
Define the meaning first. Assess quality second.

00:00:06.902 --> 00:00:10.497
Then choose a dtype, encoding, or scaling method.

00:00:10.497 --> 00:00:18.322
Finally, perform the analysis. The temptation is to let pandas or scikit-learn decide what a variable means.

00:00:18.322 --> 00:00:23.602
Instead, use software to implement a conceptual decision you can explain.

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:29.947
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:35.822
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:43.547
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.547 --> 00:00:49.542
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.542 --> 00:00:55.520
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
